# For `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .`: BuildKit prefers a dockerignore file named
# after the Dockerfile it sits beside over the root `.dockerignore`, which is written for
# the *other* Dockerfile and excludes apps/web entirely -- the opposite of what this build
# needs. Everything the web build doesn't touch, so the build context stays small and a
# change under packages/engine or apps/api never invalidates its layer cache.

.git
.github
.venv
**/.venv
packages/engine
apps/api
benchmark
tools
.logs
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache

